# The turn panel's "Opponent's last turn" and its fold: the six-timeline game (many-boards.5dr), White plays its five boards (one of them a
# jump from L-2 to L-1) and submits; Black's panel then lists White's moves. A click on a line shows that move's board and flashes
# its squares; C folds the panel away and brings it back.
record ../records/many-boards.5dr
wait 150
clicksq 3 8 d1
wait 40
clicksq 3 8 b3
wait 60
clicksq 2 8 b1
wait 40
clicksq 2 8 a3
wait 60
clicksq 1 8 d2
wait 40
clicksq 1 8 d4
wait 60
clicksq -2 8 d1
wait 40
drag 300 300 300 560 6
wait 30
hoversq -1 8 c2
wait 30
clicksq -1 8 c2
wait 80
key ENTER
wait 120
capture checklist-black-turn

# The jump: its board comes into view with the board it went to, and both squares are marked
click 1200 595
wait 30
capture checklist-opponent-move

# C folds the panel away: the boards get the width back, the HUD button says how many boards are done; C opens it again
key C
wait 40
capture checklist-collapsed
key C
wait 40
